old=r'''The received \path{os47_topology.py} was read in full and rerun on 18 November 2026 at 04:29 UTC; its unchanged source hash and current execution are recorded in \path{code/IV/replay_os47_other/current_execution.json}. Its output contains the modular coset table, integral Jacobi tuple, geometric-section uniqueness equation, fundamental-group relation matrices, full exterior and parabolic matrices, specialization indices and four clutch contractions. The received output field \path{page_index_expression=-4} is the meridian-line index \(A_U\). The positive page expression and physical index are \(4\), by the actual extending duality above. The separate current rational-function calculation in \path{code/IV/os47_sevenfold_section.py} verifies the full coordinate of \(7G\) and its ordinary pole. These executions supplement the complete geometric proof and do not replace its cap, line or orientation maps.'''
new=r'''The exact calculation in \path{code/current_audits/audit_corrections/code/independent_IV_OS47_topology.py} starts with the displayed source equation and adds its section to obtain the full coordinate of \(7G\) and the ordinary pole at \(t=-10\). Todd--Coxeter enumeration gives the based degree-nine modular coset action. The full symbolic Jacobi product yields the equation \(7(j+1)(7j+5)=0\), whose integral solution is \(j=-1\). Hermite and Smith reduction then give the integral parabolic complexes, primitive vanishing quotient and saturated finite-cap invariant lattices. Contraction with \(\ell\) has values \(1,2,2,1\); the geometrically identified specialization indices \(4,2,2,4\) give the four integral transgressions \(+1\). The program also evaluates the actual degree-four page, obtaining \((s_\delta,p_{\rm rel})=(-14,-72)\) and page expression \(4\). Its full matrices, coset-label map and section coordinates are saved in \path{code/current_audits/audit_corrections/code/independent_IV_OS47_topology.json}. The cap, Cartier-line and orientation identifications are the explicit geometric maps proved above. In particular, \(A_U=-4\) and the extending duality and inverse-clutch comparison give the physical index \(A_M=4\).'''
